# Plain-Text Notepad Editor

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M2 Core utility
Dependencies: 05_WINDOW_SHELL.todo

## Purpose

Make preparing and reading speaker notes feel like a dependable small notepad.

## Tasks

- [x] Implement standard multiline WPF text editing, selection, clipboard, undo/redo and navigation.
- [x] Add inline find, wrapping, scrolling and font size; broader theme/accessibility work remains below.
- [x] Separate text selection from dragging; synthetic mode-switch text preservation passed.
- [ ] Define and enforce the approved size limit with an explicit error, never truncation.
- [ ] Test line endings, BOM/encoding handoff, emoji, combining characters, RTL text, and IME.
- [ ] Disable app-generated note previews and audit context menus/spelling/composition surfaces.
- [ ] Keep editor state/dirty status separate from window visibility and capture setup.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Text round-trips exactly through non-edit operations and approved file encoding paths.
- [ ] Undo/redo and selection survive expected editing operations without lost or duplicated text.
- [ ] A 10,000-character synthetic note meets approved interaction budgets.
- [ ] Every context-menu/IME restriction is visible and documented, not silently broken input.
- [ ] Owner confirms readability and the plain-notepad workflow.

## Completion evidence

- Native editor/UI smoke and UTF-8/BOM/newline tests exist; owner and input/accessibility corpus remain open.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-07 - Planned; rich text, tabs, and AI are outside v1.
